From: Biscuit port <none@example.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mt8163-stp: allow skipping the ILM patch download

The WiFi firmware image writes its section 0 - 7424 bytes - to 0x0006A000,
which is inside the range this ILM patch occupies (0x00060000-0x0007F27C),
and INIT_CMD_ID_WIFI_START then tells the CONSYS MCU to jump to 0x0006A000.
The MCU is running BT firmware out of that same ILM, so on some boots it
takes an instruction-fetch abort about 1.6 ms later and both radios are
lost until a power cycle. Roughly one boot in five.

Add a writable module parameter so the patch can be left off and the cost
to Bluetooth measured. Read at probe, so toggling it and then unbinding and
rebinding soc:bluetooth applies it without a new kernel command line.

Default is unchanged behaviour.
---
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_mt8163_stp.c
@@ -1011,6 +1011,20 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The WiFi firmware download writes 7424 bytes to 0x0006A000, which sits inside
+ * this patch's range (0x00060000-0x0007F27C), and WIFI_START then tells the MCU
+ * to jump there. That is the CONSYS assert. Set to 1 to leave the ILM patch off
+ * and find out what BT loses without it.
+ *
+ * Writable and read at probe, so it can be toggled by unbinding and rebinding
+ * soc:bluetooth rather than by rebooting with a different command line.
+ */
+static bool skip_ilm_patch;
+module_param(skip_ilm_patch, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(skip_ilm_patch,
+		 "skip the ILM patch download, which the WiFi image overwrites");
+
 static int mt8163_stp_bootstrap(struct mt8163_stp *stp)
 {
 	static const struct {
@@ -1138,6 +1152,12 @@
 		 "WMT patch-download MCU clock selected at 138.67 MHz\n");
 
 	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(patches); i++) {
+		if (skip_ilm_patch && strstr(patches[i].name, "1_0_hdr")) {
+			dev_info(stp->dev,
+				 "skipping ILM patch %s (skip_ilm_patch=1)\n",
+				 patches[i].name);
+			continue;
+		}
 		ret = mt8163_stp_download_patch(stp, patches[i].name,
 						patches[i].address);
 		if (ret)
